{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 26","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the derivative of the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/6/2b68f4a6d9a7bd2bb5ca9d61230585ac69f4621a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = \\dfrac{e^{x}}{x^{2}+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"113\" height=\"40\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc80ea49ac36e0c2f0eb03eaf360f689ca8f66e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ g&#39;(x) = \\dfrac{e^{x}(x^{2}-1)}{(x^{2}+1)^{2}}  \\quad \\textbf{(B)}\\ g&#39;(x) = \\dfrac{e^{x}}{2x}  \\quad \\textbf{(C)}\\ g&#39;(x) = \\dfrac{e^{x}}{(x^{2}+1)^{2}}  \\quad \\textbf{(D)}\\ g&#39;(x) = \\dfrac{e^{x}}{x^{2}+1}  \\quad \\textbf{(E)}\\ g&#39;(x) = \\dfrac{e^{x}(x-1)^{2}}{(x^{2}+1)^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"872\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the quotient rule,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60dbdfc0e2cf3422837132623a5fbac5f973ddba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g&#39;(x) = \\frac{ \\frac{d}{dx}\\left[ e^{x} \\right] \\left( x^{2}+1 \\right) - e^{x}\\cdot \\frac{d}{dx} \\left[ x^{2} + 1 \\right]}{ \\left( x^{2}+1 \\right)^{2} } = \\frac{e^{x}\\left( x^{2}+1 \\right) - e^{x}(2x)}{\\left( x^{2}+1 \\right)^{2}}\\]\" width=\"497\" height=\"48\" />\nFactoring an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c13a313c9231ccaa699c1929a7126a313f1adbda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> out of the numerator, we notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e003a856aaf1517b9201347bfdb075209196e458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} - 2x + 1 = (x-1)^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"21\" /> to obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/5456bd051e4237f3b56ada586cc53557feada871.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{e^{x}\\left( x^{2} - 2x + 1 \\right)}{\\left( x^{2}+1 \\right)^{2}} \\implies \\boxed{ \\textbf{(E)}\\ g&#39;(x) = \\dfrac{e^{x}(x-1)^{2}}{(x^{2}+1)^{2}} }\\]\" width=\"368\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /